      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:mbi5e8'
    '|b||So it has to know the fish lost, their price, how the harm grows with more paint. Things nobody at the council can see.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:eooil6'
    '|a||Climate is the big real case. A tonne of carbon dioxide does harm all over the world, for centuries. What is that worth?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1fo11ax'
    '|a||In 2021, for instance, the US government''s working figure was fifty-one dollars a tonne.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:zggp5f'
    '|b||In 2023 its environment agency said a hundred and ninety. Or a hundred and twenty, or three hundred and forty, depending on one choice.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1i5sjff'
    '|a||The choice is how much weight to give people living a century from now. A few years earlier, counting only harm inside the US, the figure had been one to seven dollars.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1f3p4a4'
    '|b||And in 2025 the US government stopped using a figure at all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1bkp66a'
    '|b||In 1971 William Baumol and Wallace Oates suggested a way round: skip the damage estimate. Pick a target, set a tax, and raise or lower it until the target is met.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:k3ydyl'
    '|a||That reaches the target at the lowest cost. Whether it''s the right target, the tax can''t tell you.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:c6la0v'
    '|a||How sure are we? That a price on pollution cuts it is mostly agreed: British Columbia''s estimated five to fifteen percent is one of many such findings. What the right price is stays contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1keukes'
    '|a||Three new cases. Each extra car trip into a city centre does $3 of harm to others, at the efficient number of trips. What charge per trip?':
      mp3: 
